 "method": "Dimensions read on 150-500 dpi renders (pdftoppm) of the pages listed; undimensioned details (void haunches, void ledge, edge keys, chamfers, ZIPXL-2 flange curve) measured from the vector paths of the filled section drawings (PyMuPDF), scaled by the printed overall width. Published properties are the 'Grootheden prefabligger' (bare precast) columns only; composite ('samengestelde constructie') columns are recorded but not used.",
 "geometry_notes": [
  "Millimetres, origin at mid-soffit (SRP: mid of its 300 mm soffit), y up. Box voids are real polygon interiors.",
  "SKK: printed b=1480 (700-1600) / 1180 (1700-1900), top slab 170/225, bottom slab 140/175, web min. 155, joint rebate 30 deep from 315 below top. Rebate floor drawn with a 5 mm fall (315 outer, 310 inner) - taken from vector drawing.",
  "SKK void details measured from vector drawing (convention): top haunch 75 x 200, bottom chamfer 75 x 75, 20 mm ledge under the top slab whose inner edge is at x = +/-415 (b=1480) or +/-355 (b=1180); soffit corner chamfer 15 x 15. Transverse ducts (dwarssparingen h.o.h. 1200) excluded.",
  "SKK published Zb for 700-1500 is ~h/2 (+5) whereas the dimensioned outline (170 top / 140 bottom slab plus top rebate) gives Zb 8-16 mm higher; the SKK-1600 row agrees with the same outline to 0.5 mm. Pinned in tests, not fitted. Hollow self-weight/25 is 0-4 % above the model area (irregular increments, e.g. +0.2 kN/m from 1500 to 1600), so it is recorded but only loosely tested.",
  "PIQ: top 1820 + 2x40 rebate (shoulder 1900 wide, 150 tall below 350 from top), web 183 at soffit (outer faces 1750 apart), top slab 175, bottom slab 140, bottom flange b=2790 (published properties only for b=2790; range 1900-2790 not parametrised). Web taper, flange tip thickness 114 and top-flange slope, 38 mm shoulder chamfer, void haunches (75x200 top, 85x75 bottom) and 20 mm ledge measured from the vector drawing. Web outer/inner faces keep their printed widths at fixed offsets from soffit/top for other heights (convention).",
  "PIQ published Ab (1120-1210e3) exceeds hollow self-weight/25 kN/m3 (1060-1160e3), which the modelled outline matches within 1.5%; Zb published 31-38 mm below model. Pinned.",
  "SJP: 990 = 365+260+365, flange edge 85, flange top rises 20 to the stem root at 105 above soffit, stem 260 at root tapering to b at h1-h2 then vertical. Taper per side 0.225 reproduces every printed b to 0.3 mm. Root fillet (~25 R), soffit corner rounding and 4 mm edge draft omitted (convention).",
  "SJP / SJP-flex published prefab properties are 'stijfheid t.p.v. de sparingen' (stiffness at the transverse openings). They agree with the gross outline minus the opening SMEARED along the span (SJP: dia 80 at 250 c/c, centre 172 above soffit -> band 132-212 reduced by pi*40^2/(80*250) = 25.1 %; SJP-flex: 145 x 100 at 250 c/c, band 160-260 reduced by 145/250 = 58 %). The polygon is the solid gross section between openings; the smeared reduction is applied only in validation.",
  "SJP-flex: 1180 = 415+350+415, flange edge 110, stem 350 vertical to y=286 (scaled; 286.4 implied by printed b), taper 0.44 per side to b at h1-h2. Flange-top step (+20 at 143 from edge) and slope (+10 to 190 from centre) and 15 mm root chamfer scaled from vector drawing. Printed b=556 for SJP-flex 550 breaks the 0.88 mm/mm taper of every other row (582 expected); 582 implemented (areas/increments fit 582) and the printed value pinned.",
  "SRP edge beam (L): 490 = 100+90+300 at soffit level chain, 275+50+165 at top; cantilever 225 thick at the outer face, soffit 250 sloping face from (100, h1-225) to (190, h3); h2 = h1-190, h3 = h1-475 (all printed). 11 mm drip nib and 15-20 mm corner chamfers omitted (convention).",
  "SRP published Ib is 5.0-5.5 % above the transcribed outline for every size while A and Zb agree within 0.5 % / 0.6 mm; no symmetric-bending reinterpretation (principal or product-of-inertia) reproduces it. Pinned family-wide.",
  "ZIP/ZIPXL are single rail beams (railbalk) placed side by side, not multi-rib units: page 4 dimensions every rib. ZIP: 1180 = 440+300+225+215, edge 140, flange top +35 over 215, haunch +100 over 225 to the 300 stem, 230 x 35 top nib ABOVE h (h is measured to the shoulder; h1 = h-275).",
  "ZIPXL 1000-1700: 1480 = 615+250+240+375, edge 140, +68, haunch +187 to the 250 stem at 395; head 500 wide x h1 tall below h, chamfer 120 tall (105 for ZIPXL 1000) to the stem; 430 x 35 nib ABOVE h.",
  "ZIPXL 1800-2400: same bottom flange/stem; top flange 1440 wide, 40 edge, 1370 x 45 nib, h includes the nib; flange soffit is a curve spanning 190 vertically from the stem (y=h-275) to the flange edge (y=h-85), modelled as the drawn cubic Bezier (control points (125,h-275),(125,h-275),(500,h-90),(720,h-85), mirrored), sampled at 12 segments.",
  "ZIP/ZIPXL flange-edge shear-key profile (inset 24 at soffit, 7 at y=19, 0 at y=60, 32 at y=92, 15 at y=140) measured from vector drawings; stem-root fillets omitted.",
  "ZIP/ZIPXL self-weight column ('ZIP') divided by 25 kN/m3 agrees with the modelled area within 0.4 % for every size, confirming the outlines. The prefab property table does not: Ab is 2-3 % (ZIP), 4.8-7.2 % (ZIPXL 1000-1700) and 3.3-4.0 % (ZIPXL 1800-2400) above; ZIPXL 1000-1700 Zb 29-35 mm above and Ib 10-19 % above. Cause unknown (a transformed section including prestressing steel is one possibility - unverified); pinned, not fitted.",
  "ZIP 700 printed Zb=225 contradicts its own Wb (I/Wb = 16230/66 = 246 mm); model gives 246.8. Pinned as a source typo.",
  "ZIPXL 2200 printed W'b=780 contradicts I/(h-Zb) = 701180/1175 = 597; not used.",
  "Not implemented: TRN edge beam (ZIP p4; width 'minimaal 600 / maximaal 1240' variable), SJP R/TRN edge beams (p1, no properties), SKK/PIQ edge solutions (p2)."
 ],
